From Horace.Tso at pgn.com  Thu Aug  4 19:41:27 2005
From: Horace.Tso at pgn.com (Horace Tso)
Date: Thu, 04 Aug 2005 12:41:27 -0700
Subject: Re: multiple outputs in nnet
Message-ID: <s2f20d06.065@pgn.com>

If your matrix is as described, I'd use the alternative form of nnet.

 

model <- nnet(x=data[,c("x", "y", "z")], y=data[,c("F", "G", "H")], size=M1, rang=rang, decay=decay, maxit=maxit, linout=T)

Then you could see your fit with 

 

predict.nnet( model, data[,c("x", "y", "z")], type="raw" )

Cheers.

 

Horace W. Tso

