Dear all,

Using an old procedure which was working with Splus 3.4 I
was suprised to notice this new feature of Splus 6.2:

> x<-list(a=1, b=2)
> x
$a:
[1] 1

$b:
[1] 2
> names(x)
[1] "a" "b"

# i want to change the name of the first element
> names(x["a"]) <- "c"
# with this version of Splus no change
> x
$a:
[1] 1

$b:
[1] 2

With Splus 3.4 the element's name is really replaced
> names(x["a"]) <- "c"
> x
$c:
[1] 1

$b:
[1] 2

Many thanks for any comment.

