Dear list,

I am trying to produce a distribution of end-prices from a simulation of a mean reverting process.

To this end, I use the Euler discretization functions ‘euler.pcode.aux’ and ‘euler.pcode.gensim’ in an SDE to simulate my prices.

Following closely the help files, things work smoothly for the simulation of a single price track:

### S-Plus listing ###

rho.gcir<-c(0.086092008,34.73089057,0.1004521)

rho.gcir.names=c("k","mu","sigma")

ird.gcir.aux<-euler.pcode.aux(drift.expr=_expression_(k*(mu-X)-0.5*sigma^2),diffuse.expr=_expression_(sigma),rho.names=rho.gcir.names,t.per.sim=1/252,ndt=1,seed=10,X0=34.7)

gcir.sim=euler.pcode.gensim(rho=rho.gcir,n.sim=2000,n.var=1,n.burn=1000,aux=ird.gcir.aux)

###################

But, when I try to simulate multiple price paths from the same SDE either I get errors or at most price tracks which are identical.

I tried all the help-file directions to increase the dimensionality of the problem (i.e. tweaking the N,M arguments of ‘euler.pcode.aux’ and changing the expressions accordingly).

Best case scenario again was to get identical price paths, which suggests that the random seed is the ‘suspect’.

I managed to find a sideway to my problem by using an ‘lapply’ with the ‘euler.pcode.gensim’.

Clearly, there must be a way to produce multiple price paths by specifying the right syntax in the body of these new functions.

Has anyone got any views/tips with regard to the above?

Thank you,

Dimitrios Chalvatzis

