	  My understanding (and others can correct me if this is not right), is 
that in S-Plus 6.2 (and in R 2.1.1 patched), the following changes the 
name of a temporary variable created to hold 'x["a"]', and when this is 
NOT tranferred to the variable 'x':

          names(x["a"]) <- "c"

          The following works (in both S-Plus 6.2 and R 2.1.1 patched):

> x<-list(a=1, b=2)
> names(x)[1] <- "c"
> x
$c
[1] 1

$b
[1] 2

	  By the way, I would try to avoid using "c" as the name of a list 
attribute.  If you attach(x) [which is legal], then there is a potential 
conflict between "c" as the attribute of x and the concatonate function. 
 Sometimes but not always, this conflict can be resolved from the 
context.

